    "freeze_sha256": "11e8465373a0584111e08a98aaa6930fc80a58d1281e43c7025b5929526529ba",
    "blocker": "Existing active loan could lose observed domain taint when second valid submit saw live() failure then external bit restored before service. Original45 tuple was not independently approved."
  },
  "closed_findings": [
    {
      "type": "production",
      "finding": "second-submit observed-domain violation not sticky",
      "actual_RED": "submit-taint46-whole-red: one failed case, three assertions",
      "fix": "Only submit live-failure branch latches taint and first STATE cause, retains original active, quarantines and isolates owned vectors. New rejected request remains READY and unretained. Bit restoration cannot release original loan.",
      "actual_GREEN": "Same complete46, no skips; final47 also passes."
    },
    {
      "type": "external hardware model",
      "finding": "RX transfer-error helper cleared EN despite pending memory commit that could later write",
      "actual_RED": "pending-error47-model-whole-red: one external EN assertion",
      "fix": "Pending RX keeps EN1 and stop_pending; actual commit permits EN0. Driver SHA unchanged; no production bus flush added.",
      "actual_GREEN": "Same complete47, no skips."
    }
  ],
  "code_contracts_reviewed": [
    "Submit validates/admit without hardware launch; accepted launch failures retain loan. Non-SUCCESS does not retain the new request.",
    "Real RX/TX EN0 precede clear_address. M0AR/PAR/NDTR/M1AR/control readback failure retains loan. Interrupted TC cannot establish successful length, RX commit or wire idle.",
    "cstart_attempted set before unique CSTART command under saved mask is monotonic for loan. Never-issued uses actual idle baseline, not invented SUSP/EOT. Attempted refused-start remains Q without legal stop evidence.",
    "Attempted stop requires actual CSTART0 plus SUSP or finite nonzero-TSIZE EOT/TXC, independent fresh same-source quiet, bounded RX drain, SPE0/FIFO proof. Unchanged shared W1 leaves implement these operations.",
    "CPU DSB publishes previous CPU TX stores before DMA enable; it does not complete RX DMA hold. DMB and existing settle release order result/publication, not another bus-master flush.",
    "Gate observations precede DMA/SPI probes. Observed cache/domain violation is sticky through service, IRQ and newly fixed second-submit observation; restoration does not revoke original loan.",
    "Exact owned stream masks only; IRQ checks owned vector and exact IPSR. SPI IRQ preserves task EOT/SUSP evidence. Source/W1C failure isolates via real ISER0; final pending/active join precedes release.",
    "Source and NVIC isolation refusal enters masked nonreturning fault with retained borrow and observer once. Parent child kill/reap is process handling, never cleanup.",
    "First non-success cause survives late normal completion. Successful data plus real CS/source cleanup refusal latches IO; earlier cancel/deadline cause is not overwritten.",
    "CS release, SCK handoff and SPI reset precede active/endpoint clearing. Request length/result access precedes settle; provider never touches request after SETTLED. PROT_NONE oracle supports this bounded software path.",
    "Checked spans protect explicitly enumerated provider/endpoint/face/ops/System/MMIO/regions. No registry or arbitrary-address accessibility claim.",
    "PE11/GPIOE route and shared gate/vector leases are trusted static constructor lifetime preconditions, not runtime PCB or ownership authorization from matching registers."
  ],
